{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2174-03-14 13:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you've been having some neck swelling and pain since your recent surgery?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2174-03-14 13:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. I had the fistulotomy two days ago, and my throat was sore after the procedure. It got better at first, but then yesterday the pain came back worse, and now my neck is swollen and red."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2174-03-14 13:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And are you having any trouble swallowing or breathing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2174-03-14 13:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I can swallow, but it hurts. Liquids are easier. No trouble breathing, though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2174-03-14 13:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. You don’t have fever or chills?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2174-03-14 13:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, no fever. Just the pain and swelling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2174-03-14 13:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. In the ER, they did a laryngoscopy and saw some swelling in your vocal cords. They’re concerned about an infection in your right submandibular gland."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2174-03-14 13:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "The salivary gland under the jaw? What’s causing that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2174-03-14 13:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It could be related to your recent intubation. Sometimes trauma from the breathing tube can cause inflammation or blockage in the duct, leading to infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2174-03-14 13:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Ah, that makes sense. They said it was a difficult intubation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2174-03-14 13:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ve ordered a CT scan to get a better look. We’ll also start you on antibiotics just in case."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2174-03-14 13:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds good. What kind of antibiotic?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2174-03-14 13:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Clindamycin. It covers the kinds of bacteria we’re worried about, especially since you’re on immunosuppressants."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2174-03-14 13:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right, I’m on prednisone and azathioprine for my psoriatic arthritis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2174-03-14 13:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and that’s why we’re being cautious. Your immune system isn’t responding as strongly, so infections can spread faster."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2174-03-14 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your CT scan is back. It shows inflammation in the right submandibular gland, with some fluid and small pockets of air. This suggests sialadenitis — an infection of the salivary gland."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2174-03-14 14:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it serious? Could it turn into something worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2174-03-14 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "There’s a small concern it could progress to Ludwig’s angina, which is a deeper neck infection, but right now the airway is open and there’s no abscess. We’ll monitor you closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2174-03-14 14:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s reassuring. What’s the plan?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2174-03-14 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll continue clindamycin, use warm compresses, and encourage saliva flow with lemon drops or sipping water. ENT will also help express the gland to drain some fluid."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2174-03-14 14:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I can do that. And my other meds — should I keep taking them?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2174-03-14 14:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, keep taking your prednisone and azathioprine. But your rheumatologist advised holding off on starting Humira until after you finish antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2174-03-14 14:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I wasn’t planning to start it yet anyway."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2174-03-14 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also noticed some white patches in your mouth during the exam. Could be thrush, a fungal infection, common with steroid use."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2174-03-14 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I’ve had that before. Should I start antifungal treatment?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2174-03-14 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start clotrimazole troches four times a day. We’ll reassess in a day or two."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2174-03-15 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How’s the pain today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2174-03-15 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still pretty painful. The swelling hasn’t gone down much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2174-03-15 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Your white blood cell count is elevated, which means the infection is still active. We’re going to repeat the CT to see if there’s any change."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2174-03-15 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that a bad sign?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2174-03-15 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not necessarily. It just means we need to make sure the treatment is working. The repeat CT will help us decide if we need to adjust anything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2174-03-15 16:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The new CT shows the fluid collection has gotten a bit larger — it’s now a superinfected sialocele. But no abscess, and no spread to deeper spaces."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2174-03-15 16:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what does that mean for treatment?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2174-03-15 16:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll continue the same antibiotics and supportive care. ENT will come by to express the gland again. Sometimes that helps relieve pressure and speed healing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2174-03-15 16:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And the thrush? The troches seem to be helping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2174-03-15 16:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. The patches are improving. We’ll keep it on for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2174-03-16 08:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. You look better. The swelling is starting to go down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2174-03-16 08:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it feels a bit better. I can swallow more easily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2174-03-16 08:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Your WBC has come down from 16 to 14 — still high, but improving. That’s a good sign the antibiotics are working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2174-03-16 08:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good to hear. When can I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2174-03-16 08:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly tomorrow. We’ll make sure you’re eating and drinking well, and that the infection keeps improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2174-03-16 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "ENT was able to express some fluid from the gland earlier. That should help with healing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2174-03-16 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It did feel like some pressure was released."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2174-03-16 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll keep doing warm compresses and sialogogues. Also, your blood sugar has been running high — up to 248 this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2174-03-16 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, steroids do that to me. Should I adjust my glyburide?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2174-03-16 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve added glyburide to your inpatient meds. We’ll keep monitoring it. You’ll continue it at home as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2174-03-17 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Afebrile, eating, pain much improved. We’re going to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2174-03-17 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2174-03-17 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Finish the full 7-day course of clindamycin. Use warm compresses and lemon drops. Take pain meds as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2174-03-17 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the clotrimazole?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2174-03-17 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll stop that — no signs of thrush today. Follow up with ENT in a week. If swelling comes back, or you have trouble breathing, go to the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2174-03-17 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my other meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2174-03-17 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Back to your usual regimen. Prednisone at a lower dose, azathioprine, blood pressure and diabetes meds. We’ve adjusted some doses — all listed in your discharge instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2174-03-17 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I appreciate all the care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2174-03-17 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and don’t hesitate to reach out if anything changes."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2174-03-14 13:00:00",
    "admission_end": "2174-03-17 14:15:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 50-year-old male with psoriatic arthritis on chronic immunosuppression was admitted two days after an anal fistulotomy for right submandibular swelling, erythema, and pain. Initial evaluation revealed sialadenitis with imaging showing fluid and gas near the gland, raising concern for early Ludwig’s angina. He was started on clindamycin, warm compresses, sialogogues, and gland expression by ENT. A repeat CT showed worsening of the infected sialocele but no abscess or airway compromise. His symptoms improved over the next two days, white count trended down, and he became afebrile and tolerating oral intake. Thrush noted on admission improved with clotrimazole and was discontinued at discharge. He was discharged home on oral clindamycin to complete a 10-day course, with follow-up arranged with ENT and instructions to resume his baseline immunosuppressive regimen after antibiotics.",
    "problems": [
      "Sialoadenitis",
      "Candidiasis of mouth",
      "Psoriatic arthropathy",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Long-term (current) use of steroids",
      "Obesity, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
